==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|sunnentac|sunne(n)tac|lang=gmh}}, {{term|sunntac|sun(n)tac|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|sunnūntag|lang=goh}} (9th c.), from late {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*sunnōniz dagaz||day of the sun}}, a calque of Latin {{term|dies Solis|lang=la}} (4th c.). Compare Low German {{term|Sünndag|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|zondag|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|snein|lang=fy}}, English {{term|Sunday|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|søndag|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈzɔntaːk/|[ˈzɔntʰaˑkʰ]|lang=de}}
